From 06e164b139375e4197f64a2f6e170a6228ba6d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:52:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a tui notice and its chat's local wake
 deliver each event once; a gateway-owned busy chat gets tui notices in one
 tick

- local_since/created_event_id: an event written before the chat's waking local row existed stays with the
  tui row (t_01a1ce412fbf6e7f: local row created past the completion silenced it on both tui paths).
- gateway tui-owner claim follows kanban_wake_sibling (defer/cover/race) instead of skipping any chat with a
  local row; the sibling lookup covers the compression lineage (tip/root).
- legacy poller: never claims a chat the gateway owns (forwardable ledger work), and hands back notices it
  buffered when the gateway takes the chat, so no claim waits in flight for a refused turn or the reaper.
- a buffered claim whose events the wake delivered meanwhile resolves as delivered (ack, no failure, no
  re-claim): t_01a1cfb6db097701's second turn.

t_01a1cfbe6c8d46e7
